{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And now, according to your words, so it is, etc.</b> This is difficult, for this is not according to their words — for they obligated the one in whose hand the goblet is found to death, and they [made] themselves slaves. Therefore it appears [one should] say: 'according to your words' — which you decreed upon yourselves, so is the judgment of the one with whom it is found. And furthermore, I will gain for you, that you will be clear. Another explanation: 'according to your words' — that you said you are trustworthy, so it is, for the money that you found you returned. But your youngest brother, in whose trustworthiness I have not seen — he is the thief, without your knowledge. And therefore the one in whose hand the goblet is found shall be my slave, and you shall be clear.'" "<b>He shall be my slave.</b> This is difficult, for he should have said, 'he shall be a slave to my lord.' And one may answer: I must repay my lord from my own, for he was under my watch — if so, it turns out he is established as in my possession, and it is just that the thief shall be my slave."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:03.730682020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}